Rename an entry of an archive, or a folder and everything under it (zip, 7z, tar and tar
under any codec). `to` is the new full path, so a rename can also move an entry. The new
name mustn't be taken, unless only its case differs. Entries are copied without decoding,
encrypted ones included; renamed names are stored in UTF-8. A new archive is written beside
the old one and swapped in.

Usage: beezip rename [OPTIONS] <ARCHIVE> <FROM> <TO>

Arguments:
  <ARCHIVE>
          The archive

  <FROM>
          The entry or folder to rename, as listed (a folder may exist only as the parent of
          entries)

  <TO>
          Its new full path inside the archive

Options:
  -p, --password <PASSWORD>
          The password, if entry names need one (a 7z with encrypted names)

      --name-encoding <ENCODING>
          How names stored as bytes are read, so `from` matches them as listed [default: from
          config, `auto`]
          
          [possible values: auto, utf-8, cp437, cp850, cp852, cp866, cp874, cp932, cp936, cp949,
          cp950, cp1250, cp1251, cp1252, cp1253, cp1254, cp1255, cp1256, cp1257, cp1258, koi8-r,
          koi8-u, iso-8859-1, iso-8859-2, iso-8859-5, iso-8859-7, euc-jp, gb18030]

      --dry-run[=<DRY_RUN>]
          Show what would be renamed without writing anything
          
          [possible values: true, false]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --output <FORMAT>
          How to print results; ndjson streams every job event

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   One JSON document on stdout: the output, or `{"error": {...}}`
          - ndjson: Every job event as a JSON line on stdout, ending with `Finished`, `Failed` or
            `Cancelled`
          
          [default: human]

  -q, --quiet
          No progress bars or info messages; warnings still print
